1tej|n|A road or way consisting of one or more parallel series of iron or steel rails, patterned and adjusted to be tracks for the wheels of vehicles, and suitably supported on a bed or substructure. ; The road, track, etc., with all the lands, buildings, rolling stock, franchises, etc., pertaining to them and constituting one property; as, a certain railroad has been put into the hands of a receiver.	N:2445,132,5~2445,132,5
1tel|n|Reign. ; Water falling in drops from the clouds; the descent of water from the clouds in drops. ; To fall in drops from the clouds, as water; -- used mostly with it for a nominative; as, it rains. ; To fall or drop like water from the clouds; as, tears rained from their eyes.	a:105s,92,8~105s,92,8
